<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">tailoring</ansi> (skill)

Tailoring is the craft of working cloth and leather into garments — cloaks,
armor, bags, and other wearables. A skilled tailor creates light armor that
values mobility and grace over heavy protection. The skill is governed by
<ansi fg="yellow">Dexterity</ansi>, since stitching and fitting demand precision.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Requirements ━━━</ansi>

  Station:   A <ansi fg="yellow">loom</ansi> must be in the room with you.
             You'll find a loom in Pothole Coulee and most towns.
  Materials: Cloth strips, leather strips, and thread.
             Find them on the ground in the Workshop or loot from foraging.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Known Recipes ━━━</ansi>

The recipe list for tailoring is being documented as new recipes are added.
Check back soon for updates on available items.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Tailoring improves through use. Each completed craft attempt (success or
failure) has a chance to advance the skill. Tailoring progresses faster per use
than combat skills because crafting opportunities are less frequent.

There is no trainer for tailoring — practice is the only teacher.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>          Show all recipes, including tailoring ones, with status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe></ansi>      Begin crafting a tailoring recipe.
  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>              Check your current tailoring skill level.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

